.TH BURNSUITE 7 "2026-08-05" "Burn Suite 1.0" "Burn Suite Manual"
.SH NAME
burnsuite \- overview of the Burn Suite penetration testing toolkit
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Burn Suite
is a set of five standalone, homemade command\-line pentesting tools
for Kali Linux. Each tool is a single self\-contained Python script \-
none of them import from one another, so any one of them can be copied
out and run on its own. Every tool writes a readable
.B .txt
report to \fIburn_report/\fR and logs a diagnostic code for every
failure, skip, or notable empty result, so reports distinguish a real
"tested and clean" finding from an incomplete check.
.SH TOOLS
.TP
.BR burnscanner (1)
Network vulnerability scanner: host discovery, port/service scanning,
CVE lookup, Nmap vuln scripts, optional Metasploit exploitation.
Requires root for best results.
.TP
.BR burncracker (1)
WiFi handshake capture and password cracker: monitor mode, network
scanning, deauth\-assisted handshake capture, aircrack\-ng/hashcat
cracking. Requires root and a physical wireless adapter.
.TP
.BR burnrecon (1)
OSINT reconnaissance: DNS, WHOIS, subdomains, IP geolocation, Shodan,
HTTP fingerprinting, email formats, common ports. Passive, no root
required.
.TP
.BR burnweb (1)
Web application recon and weakness scanner: fingerprinting, exposed
files, directory fuzzing, nikto, TLS check, security headers. Passive
by default; active SQL injection testing is available but gated
behind an explicit typed confirmation. No root required.
.TP
.BR burnreport (1)
Cross\-tool report combiner: merges findings and diagnostics from
multiple existing reports into one summarized document. No root
required, does not scan anything itself.
.SH INSTALLATION
Place all five scripts, \fIinstall.sh\fR, \fIREADME.txt\fR, and
\fIERROR_CODES.txt\fR in the same folder, then run
.BR "sudo ./install.sh" .
This installs dependencies, registers each tool as a system command
(\fBburnscan\fR, \fBburncrack\fR, \fBburnrecon\fR, \fBburnweb\fR,
\fBburnreport\fR) via symlinks in \fI/usr/local/bin\fR, and creates the
\fIburn_report/\fR directory. Running any tool directly with
.B "python3 ./<toolname>.py"
works identically without installing.
.PP
On some systems (Kali included) \fBsudo\fR's \fIsecure_path\fR excludes
\fI/usr/local/bin\fR as a hardening default. If \fB"sudo burnscanner"\fR or
\fB"sudo burncracker"\fR reports "command not found" despite a successful
install, use the full path instead:
\fB"sudo python3 /path/to/burnsuite/burnscanner.py"\fR.
\fBinstall.sh\fR detects this and prints a note when it applies.
.SH DIAGNOSTIC CODES
Every tool logs a short code (e.g. \fBSCAN\-401\fR, \fBCRACK\-302\fR,
\fBRECON\-203\fR, \fBWEB\-406\fR) whenever a check fails, gets skipped,
or comes back empty, and every report ends with a \fBDIAGNOSTICS\fR
section listing every code that fired during that run. Codes are
categorized:
.TP
.B [HARDENED]
The check ran successfully and found nothing \- a real, reportable
negative result.
.TP
.B [INCONCLUSIVE]
The check could not complete (missing tool, timeout, rate limit,
connectivity issue). Not a security conclusion either way.
.TP
.B [ENV]
A setup/environment problem unrelated to the target.
.PP
The full reference for every code, grouped by tool, is in
.I ERROR_CODES.txt
in the suite root.
.SH TESTING
A persisted regression test suite lives in \fItests/\fR (stdlib
.BR unittest ,
no extra dependencies). Run it with:
.PP
.nf
.RS
python3 \-m unittest discover \-s tests \-p "test_*.py"
.RE
.fi
.PP
or via the wrapper script \fItests/run_tests.sh\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I burn_report/
All generated reports (auto\-created).
.TP
.I ERROR_CODES.txt
Full diagnostic code reference for all five tools.
.TP
.I README.txt
Full setup, configuration, and usage documentation.
.TP
.I shodan_api.txt
Optional Shodan API key, read by \fBburnrecon\fR.
.TP
.I install.sh
Dependency installer and system command registration script.
.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.B FOR AUTHORIZED TESTING ONLY.
Only use these tools on networks, devices, accounts, and applications
you own or have explicit written permission to test. Unauthorized use
is a federal crime under the Computer Fraud and Abuse Act (CFAA) and
equivalent laws worldwide. The authors assume no liability for misuse.
Tools with an active\-exploitation capability
(\fBburnscanner\fR's Metasploit step, \fBburnweb\fR's sqlmap step) gate
that capability behind explicit, separate confirmation for exactly
this reason.
